.SH NAME
voltkit\-trigger \- Run a hotkey action via the daemon, or directly if it isn\*(Aqt running
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvoltkit trigger\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIACTION\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a hotkey action via the daemon, or directly if it isn\*(Aqt running
.PP
Meant to be bound to a key in the desktop\*(Aqs keyboard settings or a compositor config. Results and errors are shown as desktop notifications.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIACTION\fR>

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
ocr: Extract text from a screen region
.IP \(bu 2
color: Pick a color from the screen
.IP \(bu 2
snippets: Open the snippet picker
.RE
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
A Sway or i3 binding:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBbindsym $mod+Shift+t exec voltkit trigger ocr\fR
.fi
.RE
